        question: "How do RFID wristbands prevent credential sharing or transfer?",
        answer: "Anti-transfer wristbands use a one-time closure that cannot be re-attached once removed. Attempting to cut and reattach visibly damages the closure, making it obvious to gate staff. For VIP zones, this is the primary physical anti-sharing mechanism — RFID alone does not prevent sharing if the band can be transferred intact."
